  "reason": "R1 provides strong precedent that an MTP can attain near-DFT fidelity in a closely related BCC refractory multicomponent alloy, while R2 and R20 establish that SRO can have consequential energetic or transport effects in refractory HEAs. R12 and R15 point more generally to electronic/DOS-derived thermodynamic contributions, and R3/R10 illustrate ML or accelerated computational strategies. However, none of the records proposes using an MTP for the liquid phase, replacing thermodynamic integration with MTP-to-DFT free-energy perturbation, or exploiting the low variance of MTP–DFT energy differences for melting calculations. Thus, the records point in the right direction but leave the central FEP-based intervention as a substantial new idea."
